//- "What this site is" — three cards, reusing electerm.org's feature-card grid.
//- Then the latest release called out on its own, since that is the one thing
//- most visitors actually want and the one thing this archive is not the home of.

section.features.archive-about
  .container
    .section-header
      h2 This is the electerm release archive
      p The product site is electerm.org. This site exists for one reason: past versions.
    .features-grid
      .feature-card
        .feature-icon 📚
        h3 Every version, kept
        p All #{stats.total} electerm releases since #{stats.firstYear} are archived here with their original files, sizes and release notes — nothing is pulled when a new version ships.
      .feature-card
        .feature-icon ⬇️
        h3 Download any past version
        p Open a version, pick your OS and CPU architecture, then download from GitHub or a mirror. Old glibc builds, LoongArch, RISC-V, ARMv7 and Windows 7 packages are all still here.
      .feature-card
        .feature-icon 🌐
        h3 Latest lives on electerm.org
        p For the current release, install instructions, documentation and support, use the main site — it always tracks the newest version.

section.latest-release
  .container
    .latest-card
      .latest-card-body
        span.latest-badge Latest in the archive
        h2= latest.name || ('electerm ' + latest.version)
        p.latest-meta Released #{latest.date} · #{latest.assetCount} files for Windows, macOS, Linux and Android
        p.latest-note Jump to this version's page for the full file list and its release notes, or use electerm.org for the guided download.
      .latest-card-actions
        a.hero-btn.hero-btn-primary(href='/releases/' + latest.version + '/') View &amp; download #{latest.version}
        a.hero-btn.hero-btn-secondary(href='https://electerm.org/#downloads', target='_blank', rel='noreferrer') Official download page
